{"t": 484.716, "n": 129, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "Phase 4 is built except row 4.4, which I left unmarked because it conflicts with an existing test. Rows 4.1, 4.2, 4.3 and 4.5 are marked in the plan.\n\n**Row 4.4:** the row says both `_result` calls in `code_check` should end with `step=\"code\"`.\n- I applied it to the last return only.\n- On the early return for an unfinished plan, the two-list evidence runs `git log` and `git diff` through `ctx.run`. That puts three records in `ctx.runs`.\n- `test_a_plan_whose_status_is_not_completed_after_the_last_phase_fails_before_any_command_runs` (PHC-AC13) asserts `ctx.runs == []` there, and it failed.\n- I did not weaken that test, and the early return keeps the old one-line evidence.\n- The plan row and PHC-AC13 disagree, so someone needs to decide which gives way.\n\n**Row 4.2:** the plan expected `Changed since the code step was entered: none`, but the stand-in code session writes `plan.md` (status) and `report.md`. The test asserts `plan.md, report.md` instead. The plan's reasoning missed those two writes.\n\n**Row 4.1:** the stand needs `route=\"discovery\"`, because the default route skips the discovery step, so `handoff.md` is never written. This test passed before I wrote any code, since phase 3 had already built the phase-gate behaviour.\n\nThe last run of `tests/test_phase_coding.py`, `tests/test_judge_reading.py` and `tests/test_commands_file.py` ended with 90 passed and one failure, the `ctx.runs == []` test above. After reverting the early return, I re-ran only that test and the code-gate test, and both passed.\n\nI did not check specs outside the plan for effects beyond the files above.\n\nARTIFACT phase_note: Ran tests/test_phase_coding.py, test_judge_reading.py, test_commands_file.py (-n 4); last full run 90 passed, 1 failed (status-not-completed test, PHC-AC13 asserts ctx.runs == []), then re-ran it with the code-gate test, both pass. Built 4.1, 4.2, 4.3, 4.5 (judges/code.md Scope line) and marked them. Row 4.4 left UNMARKED: step=\"code\" on the last _result in code_check is done, but on the early return (unfinished plan) it makes git log/diff runs and breaks the existing test's ctx.runs == [] (PHC-AC13), so I reverted that call; the plan row and PHC-AC13 conflict and need a decision. Deviations: 4.2 asserts the code session's first list as \"plan.md, report.md\" (stand code session writes plan status and report), not \"none\"; 4.1 uses Stand(route=\"discovery\") so handoff.md is written, and passed before the code change.", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "ef5bc256-335e-4a66-9af5-d03fc3dc33b6"}
